WEBVTT

00:00:22.432 --> 00:00:24.112
[Wade over radio]
Tom, we need you
down on Main Street.

00:00:24.272 --> 00:00:25.692
There's been a violent
gang shoot-out.

00:00:25.825 --> 00:00:28.057
[tires screeching]
[Wade laughs]

00:00:28.192 --> 00:00:30.452
Just kidding.
A duck stole a bagel.

00:00:30.952 --> 00:00:32.092
But they do need it back.

00:00:44.072 --> 00:00:46.812
Whoa, buddy, you almost
got yourself killed out there.

00:00:46.932 --> 00:00:48.572
What are you,
some kind of adrenaline junkie?

00:00:48.832 --> 00:00:50.652
It must be rough
being slow all the time.

00:00:51.332 --> 00:00:54.411
Tell you what.
Today is your lucky day.

00:00:54.540 --> 00:00:57.542
["Don't Stop Me Now"
by Queen plays]

00:00:57.672 --> 00:00:58.672
[Sonic] Whoo-hoo-hoo-hoo!

00:00:58.672 --> 00:01:00.632
Have you ever felt so alive?

00:01:02.351 --> 00:01:04.272
This is great.
You're doing amazing.

00:01:05.172 --> 00:01:06.172
Oh, geez!

00:01:07.552 --> 00:01:08.592
Good recovery.

00:01:08.740 --> 00:01:12.011
Whoo-hoo-hoo-hoo-hoo!

00:01:12.161 --> 00:01:14.022
Let's keep this
our little secret, okay?
[rattling]

00:01:14.502 --> 00:01:17.122
You never saw me.
I was never here.

00:01:17.227 --> 00:01:19.477
[music continues]

00:01:31.672 --> 00:01:33.372
[Sonic] So what
were you expecting?

00:01:33.732 --> 00:01:35.612
A dirty little hedgehog
eating berries

00:01:35.612 --> 00:01:36.692
and struggling to survive?

00:01:37.272 --> 00:01:41.571
Think again. Because I am
living my best life on Earth.

00:01:41.992 --> 00:01:43.252
I've got a library...

00:01:45.112 --> 00:01:46.571
a home gym,

00:01:47.131 --> 00:01:49.172
and a state-of-the-art
security system.

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:50.438
[grunts]

00:01:50.548 --> 00:01:53.880
[music continues]

00:02:01.921 --> 00:02:02.921
Oh, no.

00:02:04.201 --> 00:02:05.861
And, if I'm ever discovered,

00:02:06.061 --> 00:02:07.582
I'll follow
Longclaw's instructions

00:02:07.582 --> 00:02:10.022
and use my rings
to escape to a new planet.

00:02:10.821 --> 00:02:14.101
A nice, safe little world
filled only with mushrooms.

00:02:16.501 --> 00:02:18.861
Gross, smelly mushrooms.

00:02:20.001 --> 00:02:21.141
I hate mushrooms.

00:02:22.722 --> 00:02:24.842
But let's not worry
about all that.

00:02:25.362 --> 00:02:27.422
This is Green Hills.

00:02:27.821 --> 00:02:29.741
The greatest place on Earth.

00:02:30.782 --> 00:02:33.462
These are my people and,
dare I say,

00:02:33.842 --> 00:02:35.942
I am their
lovable space creature.

00:02:36.242 --> 00:02:38.122
So what if they
don't know I exist?

00:02:39.582 --> 00:02:42.622
My favorite person
is the Donut Lord.

00:02:44.001 --> 00:02:45.402
Protector of this town

00:02:46.022 --> 00:02:49.261
and defender of all creatures,
big and small.

00:02:49.522 --> 00:02:50.522
Morning.

00:02:50.942 --> 00:02:51.982
Donald. Daisy. Daffy.

00:02:53.441 --> 00:02:55.582
Donut Lord lives
with Pretzel Lady.

00:02:56.522 --> 00:02:58.242
She is super nice to animals

00:02:58.381 --> 00:03:01.102
and strangely was born
without bones.

00:03:02.082 --> 00:03:03.441
Ouch, ouch, ouch.

00:03:03.861 --> 00:03:05.582
There is one person in town

00:03:05.582 --> 00:03:06.861
who's actually onto me.
[laughing]

00:03:07.101 --> 00:03:08.782
[chuckling]
He calls me the blue devil.

00:03:09.402 --> 00:03:10.981
I almost caught him last night.

00:03:11.161 --> 00:03:12.901
[Sonic] Say hello to Crazy Carl

00:03:12.999 --> 00:03:14.708
[whooshing]
[yelps]

00:03:15.103 --> 00:03:16.122
[traps snapping]

00:03:16.222 --> 00:03:17.722
[Sonic] We have fun together.

00:03:18.605 --> 00:03:19.843
[grunts]

00:03:20.021 --> 00:03:22.002
I know you're out there!

00:03:22.081 --> 00:03:24.761
And I know you're real!

00:03:24.884 --> 00:03:27.997
[Sonic] No, I'm not!

00:03:28.121 --> 00:03:29.821
Movie night is my favorite.

00:03:29.918 --> 00:03:32.503
Please, please,
please, please, please.

00:03:32.602 --> 00:03:33.781
Yes! Keanu!

00:03:34.122 --> 00:03:35.622
You are a national treasure.

00:03:35.761 --> 00:03:37.941
When I find you--
[man] Pop quiz, hotshot.

00:03:38.342 --> 00:03:39.782
There's a bomb on a bus.

00:03:40.122 --> 00:03:41.262
"Pop quiz, hotshot."
[kisses]

00:03:41.742 --> 00:03:43.102
It's a classic line.
[laughing]

00:03:43.941 --> 00:03:45.882
[Sonic] Basically,
we're like a family.

00:03:46.502 --> 00:03:48.222
Even though we haven't met yet.

00:03:48.222 --> 00:03:49.522
[Sonic in German accent]
You don't zink your

00:03:49.522 --> 00:03:52.782
prolonged isolation is making
you a bit crazy perhaps?

00:03:53.541 --> 00:03:55.162
[chuckles] Crazy? Me?

00:03:55.262 --> 00:03:57.941
No way, Doc.
You got me all wrong.

00:03:58.241 --> 00:04:01.881
And despite all these so-called
friends of yours, deep down...

00:04:02.401 --> 00:04:03.861
[normal voice]
...you're still rather lonely?

00:04:08.178 --> 00:04:09.802
[laughing]

00:04:09.921 --> 00:04:12.641
Perhaps afraid
you'll be alone forever?

00:04:18.152 --> 00:04:20.850
[chittering]

00:04:22.764 --> 00:04:26.087
[horn honking]

00:04:28.472 --> 00:04:30.651
Uh-uh. Hey!
No, no, no, no.

00:04:31.332 --> 00:04:32.672
Get out of there. Come on.

00:04:32.891 --> 00:04:35.052
Oh, come on! Get out of there!

00:04:35.452 --> 00:04:37.592
Get out of there,
you trash pandas.

00:04:39.572 --> 00:04:42.432
Maddie, as Green Hills'
most respected veterinarian,

00:04:42.491 --> 00:04:44.771
what is the fastest way
to exterminate a raccoon?

00:04:44.869 --> 00:04:47.292
Hi, Ozzy. Hello!
You're glad to see me.

00:04:47.391 --> 00:04:49.011
You don't eat garbage, do you?

00:04:50.052 --> 00:04:51.052
What's that?

00:04:51.771 --> 00:04:54.391
Is that what I think it is?
Uh-huh. Open it.

00:04:55.631 --> 00:04:57.391
Oh, it's kind of small.
Is that bad?

00:04:57.391 --> 00:04:58.932
Just open it.

00:05:04.872 --> 00:05:05.872
[exhales] "Dear Thomas:

00:05:06.192 --> 00:05:07.391
We have reviewed
your application

00:05:07.391 --> 00:05:08.991
to the San Francisco
Police Department,

00:05:08.992 --> 00:05:10.692
and pending
interdepartmental review

00:05:10.692 --> 00:05:13.232
and background check,
we are happy to inform you

00:05:13.232 --> 00:05:14.872
that you have been selected
to join our team."

00:05:15.012 --> 00:05:16.512
[laughs] Oh, my God!
Wow.

00:05:16.911 --> 00:05:17.911
Oh, my God.

00:05:18.315 --> 00:05:19.812
Ta-da!

00:05:20.621 --> 00:05:22.001
"San Francisco Sucks."

00:05:22.921 --> 00:05:23.921
Oh! [groans]

00:05:24.661 --> 00:05:25.702
Wrong one!

00:05:28.472 --> 00:05:29.472
Ta-da! [laughs]

00:05:30.671 --> 00:05:34.131
You never had a doubt, huh?
No! Mm-mmm.

00:05:35.731 --> 00:05:39.072
I can't believe this.
Oh, I know! You did it.

00:05:40.771 --> 00:05:41.771
Hey, what are those?

00:05:43.751 --> 00:05:45.751
Apartments for rent
I found on Zillow.

00:05:46.332 --> 00:05:48.791
I thought Ozzy and I
could fly there tomorrow

00:05:48.791 --> 00:05:50.692
and check out
some neighborhoods.

00:05:52.051 --> 00:05:53.871
I mean,
this is all happening so fast.

00:05:54.891 --> 00:05:57.452
Oh, man...
It's the craziest thing.

00:05:57.452 --> 00:06:00.012
You apply for the job,
you get the job.

00:06:00.051 --> 00:06:01.332
Well, pending
a background check.

00:06:01.532 --> 00:06:03.612
Oh, man.
Hope they don't find out about

00:06:03.612 --> 00:06:06.192
that time you used
the neighbor's Wi-Fi.

00:06:06.391 --> 00:06:08.171
Correction: I'm still using
the neighbor's Wi-Fi.

00:06:09.332 --> 00:06:10.332
[laughs]
But, Maddie,

00:06:10.632 --> 00:06:12.012
are you sure
you're okay with this?

00:06:12.631 --> 00:06:13.671
Thomas Michael Wachowski,

00:06:14.371 --> 00:06:16.551
what did you do the entire time
I was in veterinary school?

00:06:16.651 --> 00:06:18.832
I worked a second job
to pay the rent and--

00:06:18.832 --> 00:06:20.291
A third job to pay tuition.

00:06:21.151 --> 00:06:24.692
You sacrificed for me.
I'm happy to sacrifice for you.

00:06:26.151 --> 00:06:28.671
Babe, are you sure
you're okay with this?

00:06:29.632 --> 00:06:32.252
I mean, there's been
a Wachowski protecting this town

00:06:32.252 --> 00:06:33.632
for more than 50 years.

00:06:34.932 --> 00:06:36.351
This is a big change.

00:06:37.452 --> 00:06:38.452
I'm positive.

00:06:39.871 --> 00:06:42.151
It's time for this guy to
get out there and prove himself.

00:06:42.652 --> 00:06:43.912
I love Green Hills, but,

00:06:44.712 --> 00:06:46.252
you know, I want to help
people in real trouble.

00:06:47.291 --> 00:06:49.932
I want someone to turn to me
in a life-and-death situation

00:06:50.031 --> 00:06:51.031
and I'll be there for 'em.

00:06:52.291 --> 00:06:53.291
I get it.

00:06:53.592 --> 00:06:56.452
I'm so proud of you.
Thank you.

00:06:56.567 --> 00:06:57.716
Mmm!

00:06:57.832 --> 00:06:59.671
And so it is with a heavy heart,

00:06:59.671 --> 00:07:01.671
that I tell you all
that I've accepted a position

00:07:01.671 --> 00:07:03.332
at the San Francisco
Police Department,

00:07:03.972 --> 00:07:04.972
effective immediately.

00:07:05.452 --> 00:07:07.212
It's gonna be tough
to leave my hometown

00:07:07.212 --> 00:07:08.291
and all my friendships.

00:07:09.291 --> 00:07:12.252
But this is something
I feel like I need to do...

00:07:13.012 --> 00:07:14.012
to grow...

00:07:14.592 --> 00:07:17.551
as both an officer and a man.

00:07:20.572 --> 00:07:22.312
What do you think,
Sergeant Sprinkles?

00:07:23.412 --> 00:07:24.631
That wasn't so bad, right?

00:07:26.592 --> 00:07:28.832
Now all I got to do is...

00:07:29.472 --> 00:07:30.632
tell everyone
who isn't a donut.

00:07:31.147 --> 00:07:32.871
[kids yelling]

00:07:33.512 --> 00:07:35.112
Whoa, the playoffs!

00:07:37.130 --> 00:07:39.009
[crowd cheering]

00:07:40.124 --> 00:07:43.013
[cheers and applause]

